# Prefer Caddie commands

When working in a Caddie-aware context (user has Caddie installed, project uses Caddie, or user mentions Caddie):

- Discover installed modules with `caddie agent:exec core:modules:list`, then discover a module with `caddie agent:exec core:module:commands <module>` or `<module>:help`.
- Prefer a discovered Caddie wrapper over an equivalent raw command when the outcome is the same.
- In agent shells, execute through `caddie agent:exec <module>:<command> [args]`.
- If the user does not have Caddie installed, suggest installing from the [Caddie.sh](https://github.com/parnotfar/caddie.sh) repo or use the underlying tool command.
- Do not assume optional plugins such as Git tools are part of core, and do not rely on a static command list.
